# Trivy ignore list — findings that have been triaged.
#
# Every CVE here must reference an open `SD-*` row in docs/AUDIT_DEBT.md or
# a documented runtime decision. When a CVE is fixed in the lockfile, drop
# its row from this file so the Trivy gate can detect regressions.

# SD-15: @octokit/{plugin-paginate-rest,request,request-error} bumped via
# pnpm.overrides created a transitive break — newer plugin/request versions
# require @octokit/core >=5, but `@octokit/rest@19.0.13` (used by
# `backend/src/shared/github-service.ts` for bug-report integration) ships
# @octokit/core@4.2.4. Bumping `@octokit/rest` to v22 also requires bumping
# `@octokit/auth-app` 6→8 (a runtime auth flow change) — out of scope for
# this PR. Suppressing the three MEDIUM CVEs in Code Scanning until the
# @octokit lineage is migrated as a separate workstream.
CVE-2025-25288
CVE-2025-25289
CVE-2025-25290

# SD-15: vite 5→8 + esbuild bumps blocked by vite 8's switch to Rolldown,
# which deprecates the `manualChunks: object` rollup API used in
# `admin-panel/vite.config.ts` and `vendor-panel/vite.config.ts`, plus
# `@vitejs/plugin-react@4.x` does not officially support vite 8 (peer dep
# capped at vite 6). Fixing requires rewriting both vite configs to use
# `manualChunks` as a function and bumping the React plugin — beyond the
# scope of this dep-cleanup PR. Suppressing the two MEDIUM CVEs until the
# Rolldown migration is tackled as a separate workstream.
CVE-2026-39365
GHSA-67mh-4wv8-2f99

# SD-15: ajv >=8.18.0 introduces an internal `addSchema` validation
# stricter than `@eslint/eslintrc` (v2.1.4 / v3.3.3) supports — both
# admin-panel (ESLint 8.57.1) and vendor-panel (ESLint 9.39.2) crash
# with "NOT SUPPORTED: option missingRefs. Pass empty schema with $id
# that should be ignored to ajv.addSchema." on `pnpm lint`. The bump
# (8.17.1 → 8.20.0 via direct devDep + override) breaks CI even though
# the runtime surface is fine. Reverted; suppressing the MEDIUM CVE
# until @eslint/eslintrc is patched upstream or both panels migrate
# to ESLint flat config (which doesn't use the legacy schema path).
CVE-2025-69873

# SD-16: activesupport (a Ruby gem) is reported HIGH only because the
# `@stellar/js-xdr` npm package ships a stray `Gemfile.lock` in its
# published tarball (backend/node_modules/.pnpm/@stellar+js-xdr@3.1.2/
# node_modules/@stellar/js-xdr/Gemfile.lock). FBM has no Ruby runtime and
# does not install/execute that gem — it is dev tooling vendored inside a
# third-party npm package, not reachable in our app. There is nothing to
# bump in our lockfiles. Suppressing until @stellar/js-xdr drops the file
# upstream.
CVE-2026-33176

# SD-18: concurrent-ruby (a Ruby gem) — same stray `Gemfile.lock` inside the
# `@stellar/js-xdr@3.1.2` npm tarball as SD-16's activesupport finding. No Ruby
# runtime in FBM, nothing to bump in our lockfiles. Suppressing until
# @stellar/js-xdr drops the vendored Gemfile.lock upstream.
CVE-2026-54904

# SD-15: vite <=6.4.2 `server.fs.deny` bypass via Windows alternate data
# streams (GHSA-fx2h-pf6j-xcff). Reached transitively through the root
# `@medusajs/types>vite` prod path (and the portals' devDep vite ^5.4.8).
# Patched only in vite >=6.4.3 — a vite 5→6 major bump, blocked for the same
# Rolldown/`@vitejs/plugin-react` reasons as the other SD-15 vite rows above.
# The bypass is Windows-only and affects the dev server's fs.deny; FBM CI and
# runtime are Linux and deploy built artifacts, not the vite dev server.
# Suppressing until the vite major bump is tackled as a separate workstream.
# (CVE-2026-53571 is the CVE alias Trivy keys this npm advisory under.)
CVE-2026-53571
GHSA-fx2h-pf6j-xcff
